{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_security_headers_securityheaders", "label": "securityHeaders()", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Kleines Helmet-artiges Buendel; jeder Header einzeln ueberschreibbar, ein vom Handler gesetzter Header gewinnt immer. Deckt den gesamten Teilbaum ab, Ablehnungen eingeschlossen.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/security-headers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_security_headers_securityheadersoptions", "label": "SecurityHeadersOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/security-headers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_security_headers_stricttransportsecurity", "label": "strictTransportSecurity()", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Der Header wird bedingungslos gesetzt \u2014 ein Browser ignoriert ihn ueber reines HTTP, ein Dev-Server ist also ein harmloser No-op, und Framework-Server sitzen ohnehin meist hinter einem TLS-terminierenden Proxy.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/security-headers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_security_headers_hstsoptions", "label": "HstsOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/security-headers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_security_headers_additive_only", "label": "Das Buendel ergaenzt nur \u2014 false entfernt nichts", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Als Middleware laeuft es auf dem auf, was das Backend ohnehin schreibt; false heisst 'diese Middleware fuegt ihn nicht hinzu', nicht 'diese Response traegt ihn nicht'. Ein Opt-out pro Teilbaum gibt es bewusst nicht, damit die backend-eigenen 404s, die Body-Parse-413s und die generische 500 abgedeckt bleiben.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/security-headers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_security_headers_csp_excluded", "label": "CSP ist bewusst nicht Teil des Buendels", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Zu app-spezifisch \u2014 konfiguriert wird sie separat mit contentSecurityPolicy.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/security-headers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_security_headers_hsts_preload_commitment", "label": "preload ist eine Verpflichtung", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "withPreload() erfordert maxAge >= 1 Jahr plus includeSubDomains (hstspreload.org-Regeln, zur Konstruktionszeit erzwungen); eine Aufnahme in die Preload-Liste ist schwer rueckgaengig zu machen.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/security-headers.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_security_headers_securityheaders", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_security_headers_securityheadersoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/http/middleware/security-headers.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_security_headers_stricttransportsecurity", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_http_middleware_security_headers_hstsoptions", "relati